---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { getAnalyticsConfig } from '../lib/analytics';
import { lastModified } from '../lib/lastmod';

// The text below describes only what this build actually ships (see src/lib/analytics.ts), so it can't
// drift from the site. Review it whenever a tool is added or removed.
const analytics = getAnalyticsConfig();
const usesAnalytics = analytics.ga.enabled || analytics.cloudflare;

const title = `Privacy | ${site.name}`;
const description =
  'How this site handles your data: the contact form, analytics and cookies, hosting, and how to change your choices or reach me.';
const path = '/privacy/';
const updated = new Date(lastModified()).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  year: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  day: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<Page title={title} description={description} path={path} crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', href: path }]}>
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="page-lead">
    <p>
      This is a personal portfolio, and it collects as little as possible. This page explains what is collected, why,
      and how to control it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Prettier would move the periods that follow links onto their own line (a visible space), so this block is hand-formatted. -->
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Contact and quote forms</h2>
    <p>If you send a message or a quote request, what you type (your name, email address, subject or project details, and the phone number, timeline and budget range if you give them) is passed to <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, a form-handling service, which delivers it to my email inbox. The forms are protected by <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, a bot check that may process technical signals such as your IP address and browser details; it only loads when you scroll to a form or start typing in it. I use what you send only to reply to you.</p>

    <h2>WhatsApp and phone</h2>
    <p>The WhatsApp buttons open a chat with me in <strong>WhatsApp</strong>, which is run by Meta. On the quote page the message is pre-filled from what you have typed in the form, so you can send the same text; you can edit it before you send, and nothing is sent to WhatsApp unless you press Send there. The phone buttons simply start a call. I use WhatsApp and phone details only to reply to you.</p>

    <h2>On-device AI</h2>
    <p>Some pages offer optional features that use the AI built into <strong>Chrome</strong> on a desktop or laptop (and, as an experimental preview, <strong>Microsoft Edge</strong>): a chat that answers questions about me and my work (the <em>Ask AI</em> button), key points of a page, suggestions for the quote form, and a check of a job description against this site. Nothing runs until you press a button. To decide whether to show the <em>Ask AI</em> button, the page asks Chrome whether the on-device model can run on your computer; that starts nothing and sends nothing. When you do, your browser runs its model on your own computer: what you type or paste into these features is processed there and is not sent to this site or to any server of mine. The first time, your browser may ask to download its model; the browser does that itself and shares the model between sites. To answer questions and check a job description, the page loads a small text file with the contents of this site from this site (<code>/ai/knowledge.json</code>). A conversation lives only on the page: it is not saved, and it is gone when you leave or press <em>Clear conversation</em>. These features do not set cookies and are not part of the analytics described below. If you then send the quote form, what you send is handled as described under contact and quote forms.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
    {analytics.ga.enabled && (
      <>
        <p>With your permission, I use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to see how the site is used: which pages are visited, roughly where visitors come from, which devices and browsers they use, and which links, downloads and the contact and quote forms they use.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>It is opt-in.</strong> Google's script is not requested, and no analytics cookies are set, unless you click <em>Accept</em> on the notice. If you decline, or your browser sends the Global Privacy Control signal, it is never loaded.</li>
          <li><strong>What it sets and records.</strong> Two first-party cookies, <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which last up to 13 months, and events such as page views, scrolling, outbound link clicks, résumé downloads, and a contact or quote form submission or a click on a WhatsApp or phone button (<code>generate_lead</code> with only the channel, never the content of your message). Google signals and ad personalisation are switched off, and no advertising features are used.</li>
          <li><strong>Where it goes.</strong> Google processes this data on its servers, which can be outside the UAE and the EU (see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses data</a>). Google Analytics keeps event data for the retention period set on the property, with a maximum of 14 months.</li>
          <li><strong>Changing your mind.</strong> Use the <em>Privacy choices</em> button in the footer at any time. Withdrawing consent stops measurement and deletes the analytics cookies.</li>
        </ul>
      </>
    )}
    {analytics.cloudflare && (
      <p>I also use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to count visits. According to Cloudflare it does not use cookies or other client-side storage, and does not fingerprint or track you across sites, so it runs without a consent prompt.</p>
    )}
    {!usesAnalytics && (
      <p>This site does not currently use analytics, and it does not set tracking cookies. Fonts and icons are served from this site, not from third parties.</p>
    )}

    <h2>IELTS Band Builder</h2>
    <p>The free IELTS Band Builder app at <a href="/ielts/">shakoorattari.com/ielts</a> sets no cookies and has no advertising.{usesAnalytics && ' The analytics described above do not run in it.'} Your progress, saved essays and drafts are kept in your own browser (<code>localStorage</code>) and are not sent to me. If you choose to turn on sync between devices, the app talks directly from your browser to <strong>GitHub</strong>'s Gist service with a personal access token that you provide and that stays in that browser; I never see the token or your data.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. Like any web host, GitHub may process technical request data such as IP addresses in its server logs (see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>).</p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>You can control cookies in your browser settings, and the site honours the Global Privacy Control signal. To ask what I hold about you from the contact or quote forms, or to have it deleted, email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>{site.name}, {site.locationLabel}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

    <p><small>Last updated {updated}.</small></p>
  </div>
</Page>
